version: v1alpha1
metadata:
  name: frr
  version: "${TALOS_VERSION}-${FRR_VERSION}-${EXTENSION_REVISION}"
  author: Marco Tollini
  description: |
    FRRouting (FRR) system extension for Talos Linux.

    Provides zebra (kernel route installation), bgpd (BGP) and bfdd (BFD)
    as a Talos extension service. mgmtd and staticd are also enabled since
    FRR requires them to always run. All other daemons are disabled by
    default and can be enabled by overriding /etc/frr/daemons via an
    ExtensionServiceConfig.

    FRR itself ships no static routing configuration: /etc/frr/frr.conf is
    an inert placeholder until it is overridden at runtime via a Talos
    ExtensionServiceConfig (applied with `talosctl patch machineconfig`).

    See https://github.com/marcotollini/frr-for-talos for configuration
    instructions.
  compatibility:
    talos:
      version: ">= v1.11.0"
